onse vehicle being sent  to your location your nearest ane  department is at Southend hospital on  pretty well chase westcliff-on-sea Essex  SS 00 are Y and their telephone number  is 0 1 702 for 355 double five  a guide with up-to-date information  about local health care services is  available on the NHS south east essex  website at WWE NHS UK the e booklet  entitled your guide to local health  services 2010-11 published by NHS south  east essex contains lots of useful  contact numbers including information  about local NHS dentists GP practices  pharmacies and opticians a variety of  other useful telephone numbers for local  health services and help lines are also  featured in the guide the guide can be  downloaded and printed at local  libraries who do not have internet  internet access at home information  about how NHS south east essex spends  its budget is included you can also find  out more about how you can have your say  when it comes to local health care  services by sharing feedback and being  more involved in the decision-making  process the chairman of NHS south east  essex katherine kurt said there are so  many local health services available  across southeast essex and by having all  the information in one place not only  can people get quick access to their GP  or dentists firm number they can also  find out more about a wealth of other  local services that might be of interest  to them and here's how you can get your  copy of the guide to health services  online you log on to www seu NHS UK on  the front page go to click here to  download your guide 2010-11 once you've  clicked the guide should automatically  appear and as we've said before if you  don't have access to the internet go to  your local library and they can download  a copy for you  the initiative shown by two hotly  teenagers who went to the aid of an  elderly lady in distress has been  recognized by the police and Rochford  district communities 50 partnerships  known as CSP greens would academy  students amy castleton and megan  anderson both 16 have each been  presented with the letter of  commendation from district commander in  chief inspector Glen Wesley and 15 pound  iTunes vouchers by the CSP the girls  were approached by the elderly lady in  white hart lane hockley the woman  confused and disorientated after  mistakenly alighting from a bus had lost  her bag containing her bus passed a  mobile phone and could not remember  where she lived she asked us where the  community hall was but neither of us  knew what she meant so we tried to  direct her to a nearby church but she  didn't really understand explained Amy  and Megan after several attempts to find  someone to help or who might know or  recognize the woman the girls took her  to hockley library and the police were  called police Community Support Officer  John Dennis said the girls showed great  presence of mind in not abandoning the  lady but getting her to a place of  safety fortunately she was later able to  recall the name of the care home which  allowed us to pinpoint its location and  have someone collector  rochford District Council Essex Police  and the CPS have joined forces in a new  initiative to tackle anti-social  behavior and nuisance in hockley working  together the partners have secured a  dispersal order for large areas of the  town giving police proactive powers to  defuse potential nuisance behavior  officers can disperse groups of two or  more people congregating in designated  dispersal areas including Maryland's  Nature Reserve and woods plumber amount  and the grounds of bets would community  center anyone refusing to leave when  asked by the officers or who returns  within 24 hours commits an offense and  can be arrested the order also gives  police the power to take children under  16 years old back home if stopped in a  designated area after 9pm and not  accompanied by a responsible adult in  the month following the introduction of  the order on monday the 